-- title:
--   Bounded rigidification exponent over Noetherian local bases
-- statement:
--   The statement is an assertion about the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison datum, set up by a long list of hypotheses which are grouped and named below; the conclusion is a bound, uniform in the base, for the isogeny exponent of a rigidification of a fake elliptic curve in terms of the exponent of the associated rigidified special formal module.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Two distinct primes $r$ and $\bar r$, and a squarefree $N \neq 0$ divisible by neither ($hrr$, $hrN$, $hrbarN$, $hN$). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring ($hdvr$) with an irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology ($hcomplete$), with residue ring of cardinality $r$ ($hres$) and $(r) = (\pi)$ ($hunr$); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (`Onr`) over $\mathcal{O}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$ ($hOnr\_complete$), that ideal being maximal ($hOnr\_max$), every element satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ ($hOnr\_alg$), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ ($hOnr\_closed$), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ ($hFr$). A monoid homomorphism $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by $hvdet$: $v_{\det}(g) = n$ precisely when $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal{O}^{\times}$.
--
--   **The indefinite algebra and its moduli.** Rationals $a, b$ with $hB$: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb{Z}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ ($h\Lambda$), containing every rational integer ($h\Lambda\mathbb{Z}$); a map $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathrm{Zp2}\,r \times \mathrm{Zp2}\,r$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` ($hcoord$: six clauses — additivity, $1 \mapsto (1,0)$, the twisted multiplicativity rule involving $r$ and the Witt Frobenius, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and a trace condition). A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}$ with structure morphism $f$ and a point map $\mathrm{pt}$ which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure ($h\mathcal{X}$, five clauses: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ ($hn$, $hrn$, $hrbarn$, $hnN$); a fine moduli space $M$, $f_M$, $\mathrm{pt}_F$ for full level-$n$ structures ($hM$, four clauses) carrying a level-twist action of a group $G$ through $\rho$ and labels $\chi$ ($h\rho$, seven clauses: the automorphisms lie over the base, they realise twists, and the labels are multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\mathcal{O}$ ($hp$), invariant under $G$ ($h\rho p$) and compatible with the point maps ($hp\_pt$). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$, $g_\ell$, $\mathrm{pt}_T$ for curves with extra $\ell$-level ($h\mathcal{Y}$) together with the two degeneracy morphisms $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\mathcal{O}$ ($hd_0f$, $hd_1f$) and their modular descriptions: $d_0$ forgets the extra level ($hd_0$) and $d_1$ records the $\ell$-isogeny quotient ($hd_1$). Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X}$ over $\mathcal{O}$ ($harf$, $harbarf$) with modular descriptions on $r$- and $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotients ($har$, $harbar$).
--
--   **The definite algebra and the arithmetic group.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with $hdef$: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \otimes \mathbb{Q}_v$ a division algebra exactly at the place containing $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$ ($h\Lambda_1$, $hR_1$, $hR\Lambda_1$); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ ($hn_1$) such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ ($hS_1$); an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ ($h\iota_0$); the height-one prime $v$ containing $r$ ($hv$). A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ equal to the group of units integral away from $v$ for $R_1$ ($h\Gamma t$). Families $s_\ell$ (global units) and $\mathit{sf}_\ell$ (adelic units) indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ with $hs$ (four clauses): the component of $\mathit{sf}_\ell$ at every place not containing $r$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$; its component at the places containing $r$ is $1$; the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $\mathit{sf}_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet` $\Lambda_1\,(R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$. The groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ ($h\Gamma t\ell$), and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ ($hwbar$).
--
--   **The special fibre package.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ over that ring (a two-dimensional commutative formal group with $\mathrm{Zp2}\,r$-action and a uniformiser endomorphism) of height $4$ ($hX_0$), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and $hA_0$: these present $A_0$ as a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Endomorphism families $e, e'$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$ with $e_\gamma$ over the base ($he$) and degrees $\deg \gamma$, subject to: $hE1$ (each pair $(e_\gamma, e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ preserving level); $hE1mul$ (multiplicativity in $\gamma$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$); $hE1sc$ (for $\gamma$ a rational integral scalar $c$, $e_\gamma$ is multiplication by $c$ up to powers of $r$); $hE1'$ (conversely, if $e_\gamma$ is multiplication by a positive integer up to a power of $r$, then $\gamma$ is a scalar); $hE2$ (for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the action and uniformiser endomorphisms of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ admits an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser inducing $e_\gamma$ on the formal coordinates and with image $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$); $hE3$ (each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ admits a labelling $\mathrm{lab} : \Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ computing the action of $e_\gamma$ on the structure, multiplicative modulo $n$ and scalar on scalars modulo $n$); $hE4$ (over any algebraically closed field, any $r$-power-degree level-preserving isogeny pair of a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$). An order $R_2 \leq R_1$ ($hR_2$, $hR_2o$) with every element of $R_1$ carried into $R_2$ by a power of $r$ ($hR_2r$), together with endomorphisms $\hat e_x$ over the base ($h\hat e$) satisfying: $hE5a$ (additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of level); $hE5b1$, $hE5b2$, $hE5b3$ (unit, multiplicativity, and integers acting as multiplication); $hE5c$ ($\hat e_{x^{*}} \circ \hat e_x$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$); $hE5d$ (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$, up to powers of $r$); $hE5e$ (the version of $hE2$ realising $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$ simultaneously by a single $g$).
--
--   **The Drinfeld side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathrm{Zp2}\,r \to \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ ($h\Phi$) and of height $4$ ($h\Phi 4$); a moduli package $MD$ over $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf ($hMD$); a family $\eta$ assigning to each rigidified object over a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent a point of $MD$, with $h\eta$ (three clauses): on admissible objects over Noetherian bases $\eta$ separates exactly the isomorphism classes, $\eta$ commutes with base change of admissible objects, and every point of $MD(B)$ is, over a Zariski cover of $\mathrm{Spec}\,B$ by localisations, the image under $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object. An injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action and uniformiser endomorphisms of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal{O})$ through a fixed power $r^m$ in both directions ($hE_0$). A family $eD$ identifying, for Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, the points of the functor $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal{O}\,MD$ with pairs consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum for $(K_0,\pi)$ over $B$, natural in $B$ ($hnatD$), bijective ($hbijD$), with first component the structure map ($hfstD$), intertwining the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on moduli points with the $v_{\det}$-twisted action on Deligne data ($hGLD$), sending $\pi$-translates to the Frobenius twist of the first component with unchanged datum ($hPiD$), and such that $\pi$-translates always exist ($hPiexD$). A ring homomorphism $\kappa : \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi \to \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ compatible with the quotient maps ($h\kappa$); an integer $n_0$ and a two-variable series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ ($h\beta_0$). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **The $\bar w$-package.** A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ with morphisms $a_w, a_w'$ realising the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ ($hALw$), and $b_w, b_w'$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ back to $A_0$ ($hBSw$) preserving level ($hBSwlev$), the composite $a_w \circ b_w$ being matched through the formal coordinates with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to powers of $r$, simultaneously with the matching of $hE2$ for $\Gamma_t$ ($hJOINTw$).
--
--   **The comparison map.** A family $\Xi$ assigning to each Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and each rigidified fake elliptic curve over $(B,\psi)$ a point of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.GPoint}\,\mathcal{O}\,MD$ over $B$, subject to: $h\Xi leg$ (over a base with no non-trivial idempotents, the structure map component of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{k} \circ \psi$); $h\Xi nat$ (compatibility with base change of rigidifications); $h\Xi iso$ (invariance under isomorphisms of the underlying curves which are compatible with the rigidifications up to $r$-power scalars); $h\Xi def$ (over a base with no non-trivial idempotents and $r$ nilpotent, for any presentation of the curve as a formal module by $(X,\theta)$ there exist $j \leq 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, transporting the rigidification along $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, admissible for the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$, and with $\Xi$ equal to the point built from that twist and $\eta(t)$). Finally an element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with $heq\Gamma$ (translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds, up to an integral power of the scalar $r$, to the action of $g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ on the associated $\Xi$-points) and $heqW$ (the same for the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner quotient and $\iota_0(\bar w)$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $N_b \in \mathbb{N}$ there exists $d_N \in \mathbb{N}$ with the following property. Let $S$ be a Noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent ($hS$), let $\psi_S : \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism, let $x = (E, \rho)$ be a rigidified fake elliptic curve over $(S, \psi_S)$ relative to $A_0$, and let $t$ be a rigidified formal module over $S$ relative to $\Phi$ (so $t$ consists of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $t.X$ over $S$, an exponent $t.n$, and a series $t.\rho$ over $S/rS$). Assume that $t$ is admissible for $\iota$ and the ring map underlying the structure component of $\Xi\,S\,\psi_S\,hS\,x$ (that is: $t.X$ is special for that structure map, $t.X$ has height $4$, and $t.\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4\,t.n$ from the reduction of $\Phi$ to the reduction of $t.X$), that $\eta$ applied to $t$ over that structure map equals the moduli point of $\Xi\,S\,\psi_S\,hS\,x$, and that $t.n \leq N_b$. Then there exists a rigidification $\rho'$ of the curve $x.1$ over $(S,\psi_S)$ relative to $A_0$ such that, first, $\rho'.d \leq d_N$, and second, $\rho'$ is equivalent to the given rigidification $x.2$ in the sense of `Rigidification.Equiv` with respect to $h\Lambda\mathbb{Z}$: there are morphisms $u : \rho'.E_b.A \to x.2.E_b.A$ and $u_A : \rho'.A_b.A \to x.2.A_b.A$ which form a comparison (each exhibits the target as a pullback along the identity of $S/\pi$ of the source in the sense of `IsPullbackVia`, and they are compatible with the structure morphisms $g_b$ and $g_A$), and there exist $i, j \in \mathbb{N}$ with
--   $$u \,;\, x.2.\varphi \,;\, x.2.A_b.\mathrm{act}(r^{i}) \;=\; \rho'.\varphi \,;\, u_A \,;\, x.2.A_b.\mathrm{act}(r^{j}),$$
--   composites being read in diagrammatic order. Thus the isogeny exponent $d$ of a rigidification may be bounded, uniformly in the Noetherian local base $S$, in the structure map $\psi_S$, in the curve and in $t$, by a quantity depending only on the bound $N_b$ for $t.n$ and on the ambient data.
--
--   This is the local-base form of the boundedness step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between rigidified fake elliptic curves in characteristic dividing $r$ and Drinfeld's special formal modules: it converts a bound on the exponent $t.n$ of the rigidified formal module attached to a point by $\Xi$ into a bound on the isogeny exponent $d$ of a rigidification of the curve, after replacing the rigidification by an equivalent one. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.exists_le_equiv_of_inEdgeChart_of_isLocalRing`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.exists_le_equiv_of_inEdgeChart_of_isLocalRing), where the exhaustion of the formal upper half plane by edge charts supplies the required bound on $t.n$.
